# Dependency Boundaries

## Allowed

- `apps → packages`
- `design-tokens → ui-web`, `design-tokens → ui-native`
- `types → api | state | validation`
- `api → state`, `auth → state`
- `utils`, `constants`, `types` are leaf-ish and broadly consumable.

## Forbidden

- `apps → apps` (never).
- `ui-web | ui-native → api` (UI must not know about API/business domain).
- `ui-* → state` (Redux) or business domains.
- `utils → react` (utils stays framework-agnostic).
- `constants | types → react`.
- `generated → manually maintained business logic`.
- Deep imports into another package's internals. Use the package public entry point only
  (`@azes/<pkg>` or controlled subpaths). Never `@azes/<pkg>/src/...`.

## Rules for agents

- Do not add a dependency that violates the graph above.
- Do not introduce a new package to work around a boundary; fix the design.
- When practical, enforce with ESLint import boundaries (`tooling/eslint`).
- Consult `docs/architecture/dependency-graph.md` and `docs/development/dependency-rules.md`.
